# Git workflow (Bnood)

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| **`develop`** | Daily integration. `feature/*` and `fix/*` land here. |
| **`staging`** | QA / test builds. Receives merges from `develop` only. |
| **`main`** | Production. Receives merges from `staging` only. Release tags `v*` are created on `main` only. |
| **`feature/<name>`** | Branch from `develop` → merge back to `develop` (`--no-ff`). |
| **`fix/<name>`** | Branch from `develop` → merge back to `develop` (`--no-ff`). |
| **`hotfix/<name>`** | Branch from `main` → merge to **`main`**, **`staging`**, and **`develop`** (in that order). |

Retired: `migration/remote` — do not use.

## Promotion

```
feature/*, fix/*  →  develop  →  staging  →  main  →  tag vX.Y.Z
```

- **No direct commits** on `main` or `staging` (merge commits only).
- **QA builds:** merge `develop` → `staging` when a test build is needed.
- **Production:** merge `staging` → `main`, then tag on `main` when the owner approves (tags trigger Codemagic — see `release-ci.mdc`).

## Hotfix

1. Branch `hotfix/<name>` from `main`.
2. Merge to `main` (production fix).
3. Merge `main` into `staging` (or merge hotfix branch to `staging` with same commit).
4. Merge into `develop` so integration branch stays current.

## Agent / automation constraints

- Do not `git push --force` or `reset --hard` on shared branches.
- Do not push `v*` tags unless the owner explicitly asks.
- Never commit secrets — see `release-ci.mdc` safety section.